Olissis	A legendary daughter of Imimorûl and sister of Tsonos.
Omiri urs Xunnurit	The lame daughter of Xunnurit and wife of Yursalka.
Omirji	A Kianene Grandee and follower of Fanayal ab Kascamandri.
Omrain	The first woman according to The Chronicle of the Tusk.
Onkis	The goddess of hope and aspiration.
Ontillas	A near antique Ceneian satirist best known for On the Folly of Men.
Opparitha	A near antique Cengemian moralist best known for On the Carnal.
Opsara	A Kianene slave who served as the infant Anasûrimbor Moënghus II's wet nurse.
Oresh	A historical figure in The Chronicle of the Tusk and youngest son of Angeshraël and Esmenet.
Orosis	Possibly the god of sleep.
Orra	A plump scullery slave of the House Gaunum household.
Orsuleese the Faster|Orsuleese	A Sakarpi hero famed for racing on foot from the Pale to the Lonely City to give warning of a vast mobbing.
Orsuwick	An Ordealman and Baron of Low Kalt.
Osilwas	A member of the Stone Hags.
Osseoratha	A Far Antique king of Trysë associated with overthrowing the Cond Yoke.
Lord Ostaroot	A Sakarpi nobleman and High Boonsman of King Varalt Harweel II.
Ostaroot Tasweer	The son of Lord Ostaroot.
Othkut	A Scylvendi warrior who fought in the Battle of Kiyuth.
Ouras	A sorcerer of the Imperial Saik during the Holy War.
Outhrata	A famed Sohonc metaphysician and central figure of the Gnostic Renaissance.
Oxwora	A member of the Skin Eaters and renegade son of Yalgrota Sranchammer.
